From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pavel Sokolov <pavel@sokolov.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:24:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Hold mqttasync_mutex in MQTTAsync_connect until the
 CONNECT is queued #1714

MQTTAsync_connect took mqttasync_mutex only around starting the send and
receive threads, and wrote the client's connect options, its Clients
fields and the global retry interval without it.  The send thread reads
them holding the mutex (MQTTAsync_checkTimeouts, MQTTAsync_retry), and
when it is already running for another client it can do so while they
are being written: a data race ThreadSanitizer reports.

The mutex is now taken before the first of those writes and released at
the exit, after MQTTAsync_addCommand, which takes mqttcommand_mutex
inside it in the order MQTTAsync_processCommand uses.  As before, it is
not taken when MQTTAsync_connect is called from a callback on the send
or receive thread, which already holds it.

Signed-off-by: Pavel Sokolov <pavel@sokolov.me>
---
 src/MQTTAsync.c | 21 ++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/MQTTAsync.c b/src/MQTTAsync.c
index 2981c2f..5653b18 100644
--- a/src/MQTTAsync.c
+++ b/src/MQTTAsync.c
@@ -664,6 +664,16 @@ int MQTTAsync_connect(MQTTAsync handle, const MQTTAsync_connectOptions* options)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* don't lock async mutex if we are being called from a callback.  Otherwise it is held
+	 * until the CONNECT is queued: the send and receive threads read the client's state
+	 * written below holding it, and they may already be running for another client. */
+	thread_id = Paho_thread_getid();
+	if (thread_id != sendThread_id && thread_id != receiveThread_id)
+	{
+		MQTTAsync_lock_mutex(mqttasync_mutex);
+		locked = 1;
+	}
+
 	m->connect.onSuccess = options->onSuccess;
 	m->connect.onFailure = options->onFailure;
 	if (options->struct_version >= 6)
@@ -674,13 +684,6 @@ int MQTTAsync_connect(MQTTAsync handle, const MQTTAsync_connectOptions* options)
 	m->connect.context = options->context;
 	m->connectTimeout = options->connectTimeout;
 
-	/* don't lock async mutex if we are being called from a callback */
-	thread_id = Paho_thread_getid();
-	if (thread_id != sendThread_id && thread_id != receiveThread_id)
-	{
-		MQTTAsync_lock_mutex(mqttasync_mutex);
-		locked = 1;
-	}
 	MQTTAsync_tostop = 0;
 	if (sendThread_state != STARTING && sendThread_state != RUNNING)
 	{
@@ -692,8 +695,6 @@ int MQTTAsync_connect(MQTTAsync handle, const MQTTAsync_connectOptions* options)
 		receiveThread_state = STARTING;
 		Paho_thread_start(MQTTAsync_receiveThread, handle);
 	}
-	if (locked)
-		MQTTAsync_unlock_mutex(mqttasync_mutex);
 
 	m->c->keepAliveInterval = m->c->savedKeepAliveInterval = options->keepAliveInterval;
 	setRetryLoopInterval(options->keepAliveInterval);
@@ -958,6 +959,8 @@ int MQTTAsync_connect(MQTTAsync handle, const MQTTAsync_connectOptions* options)
 	rc = MQTTAsync_addCommand(conn, sizeof(conn));
 
 exit:
+	if (locked)
+		MQTTAsync_unlock_mutex(mqttasync_mutex);
 	FUNC_EXIT_RC(rc);
 	return rc;
 }
